   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Progress Toward Outcome: The cable infrastructure to connect Kiritimati island in Kiribati was completed in July 2022. The cable company, BNL is working on establishing additional infrastructure to provide access points for local telecom operators. Some identified savings from the grant is being reallocated to prioritize activities to make the cable operational in order for BNL to carry out commercial traffic and to generate revenue. The expected date for the cable to be ready for service&apos; is end of 2023.

Nauru component of the project was cancelled March 2022.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Some results are in the Audited Project Financial Statements | Apr 2024: https://www.adb.org/sites/default/files/project-documents/50348/50348-001-apfs-en_2.pdf</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: The Southern Cross NEXT Cable system was formally announced as Ready-for-Service by Southern Cross on 1st July 2022.SX and BNL signed the Provisional Acceptance Certificate on 30th November 2021.Installation works in Kiritimati continued with the installation of equipment by ASN and Southern Cross until June 2022. Training of BNL staff was also conducted over this period.All installation works, testing and commissioning works have been completed in Kiritimati, all that remains is the clearance of some construction defects mainly associated with theCLS building module. Southern Cross is working with the building supplier (DXN) and BNL technical staff on the ground to clear these defects.SX has advised that RFPA for the marine segment provided by ASN occurred on 3 May 2022, SX is now testing the integrated system, including SLTE, leading to currently advised Ready For Service date of 30 June 2022. Following RFS, customers can be connected and so the first traffic can then flow subject to finalization of contractual agreements.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
